able access coordinator."},{"text":"they ran the studio, trained the volunteers,"},{"text":"scheduled the time slots,"},{"text":"and watched everything that aired."},{"text":"everything."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-025","slides":[{"text":"your cable bill funded this."},{"text":"a few cents per subscriber per month"},{"text":"went to the local media center"},{"text":"so anyone in town could make a show."},{"text":"you're welcome."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-026","slides":[{"text":"between 1984 and 2005"},{"text":"every town in america with a cable franchise"},{"text":"had a channel nobody watched"},{"text":"where anything could happen."},{"text":"you're watching what happened."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-027","slides":[{"text":"it is 2 am."},{"text":"you cannot sleep."},{"text":"channel 14 has something on."},{"text":"it has always had something on."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-028","slides":[{"text":"to use the community access studio"},{"text":"you had to take a six-week training course."},{"text":"camera operation. lighting. audio. basic editing."},{"text":"some people took the course"},{"text":"and made a show that ran for fifteen years."},{"text":"some people took the course"},{"text":"and were never seen again."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-029","slides":[{"text":"the studio is someone's garage."},{"text":"they've taped over the address."},{"text":"the neighbors know."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-030","slides":[{"text":"the beautiful thing about public access"},{"text":"is that no one could say no."},{"text":"no executive. no focus group. no network note."},{"text":"if you had an idea and a vhs tape"},{"text":"you had a show."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-031","slides":[{"text":"every public access station had a guy"},{"text":"who knew everything about the equipment."},{"text":"he was there when you arrived."},{"text":"he was there when you left."},{"text":"nobody hired him."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-032","slides":[{"text":"manhattan neighborhood network"},{"text":"operated four public access channels"},{"text":"in the most expensive city on earth."},{"text":"anyone who lived in manhattan"},{"text":"could walk in off the street"},{"text":"and leave with their own television show."},{"text":"some of them should have kept walking."},{"text":"most of them were exactly right."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-033","slides":[{"text":"nobody planned to watch public access."},{"text":"you were flipping channels at 2 am."},{"text":"you stopped because something was happening"},{"text":"that you'd never seen on television before."},{"text":"and would never see again."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-034","slides":[{"text":"the telecommunications act of 1996"},{"text":"started pulling the money out of public access."},{"text":"by 2005 most stations were running on fumes."},{"text":"by 2015 half of them were gone."},{"text":"the channels that carried the weirdest,"},{"text":"most human content in television history"},{"text":"were quietly defunded"},{"text":"and nobody noticed"},{"text":"because nobody was watching."},{"text":"except the people who were always watching."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-035","slides":[{"text":"this aired at 2 am on a tuesday"},{"text":"on a channel most people"},{"text":"didn't know they had."},{"text":"someone was watching."},{"text":"someone is always watching."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-036","slides":[{"text":"in the vhs era you didn't even need the studio."},{"text":"you could record your show at home"},{"text":"on a camcorder in your living room,"},{"text":"drop the tape off at the station,"},{"text":"and it would air that week."},{"text":"someone else would be watching your living room."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-037","slides":[{"text":"it's the part of the night"},{"text":"where everything on television"},{"text":"was made by someone"},{"text":"who couldn't sleep either."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-038","slides":[{"text":"the only thing public access couldn't air"},{"text":"was commercial advertising."},{"text":"everything else was fair game."},{"text":"puppet shows. political rants. yoga."},{"text":"a man in a chair reading the phone book."},{"text":"all of it. every minute of it."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-039","slides":[{"text":"some public access hosts became legends."},{"text":"not famous. legends."},{"text":"the kind of person strangers recognized at the bodega"},{"text":"at midnight and said \"I watch your show.\""},{"text":"no manager. no agent. no industry."},{"text":"just a person and a camera"},{"text":"and a following that existed entirely after 11 pm."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-040","slides":[{"text":"the cooking show that isn't about cooking."},{"text":"the comedy show that isn't about comedy."},{"text":"the variety show that has no variety."},{"text":"everything is exactly as described."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-041","slides":[{"text":"there were two kinds of public access shows."},{"text":"the kind where they knew what they were doing."},{"text":"and the kind where they absolutely did not."},{"text":"both were essential."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-042","slides":[{"text":"there is no pledge drive on public access."},{"text":"nobody is asking you to call in and donate."},{"text":"nobody is asking you for anything."},{"text":"just your attention. just for an hour."},{"text":"just on a channel you didn't know you had."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-043","slides":[{"text":"in most cable systems"},{"text":"the public access channel was somewhere"},{"text":"between 14 and 20 on the dial."},{"text":"low enough that you'd stumble across it."},{"text":"high enough that you'd wonder"},{"text":"how long it had been there."},{"text":"every town had one."},{"text":"yours had one."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-044","slides":[{"text":"before the internet"},{"text":"the only way an ordinary person"},{"text":"could broadcast to strangers"},{"text":"was public access television."},{"text":"the only barrier was showing up."},{"text":"a lot of people showed up."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-045","slides":[{"text":"someone recorded these."},{"text":"on a vhs tape. in their living room."},{"text":"they pressed record because they couldn't believe"},{"text":"what was on television."},{"text":"neither can we."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-046","slides":[{"text":"we've been watching this stuff for years."},{"text":"it doesn't get less weird."},{"text":"it gets more human."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-047","slides":[{"text":"this is what television looks like"},{"text":"when nobody is trying to sell you anything."},{"text":"just people in rooms"},{"text":"doing what they would have done anyway"},{"text":"whether the camera was on or not."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-048","slides":[{"text":"most public access was never archived."},{"text":"the tapes were reused. recorded over. thrown out."},{"text":"what survived is a fraction of a fraction"},{"text":"of what people made."},{"text":"you're watching what survived."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-049","slides":[{"text":"the people who made public access television"},{"text":"were not trying to get famous."},{"text":"they were not trying to get noticed."},{"text":"they were trying to make something."},{"text":"and they did. every week. for years."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-050","slides":[{"text":"there are thousands of hours of public access"},{"text":"sitting in archives nobody visits."},{"text":"we visit."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-051","slides":[{"text":"every one of these shows"},{"text":"was someone's favorite hour of the week."},{"text":"the hour they got to be on television."},{"text":"the hour it was their channel."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-052","slides":[{"text":"the tracking lines. the color bleed."},{"text":"the audio that clips when someone laughs too loud."},{"text":"this is what television sounded like"},{"text":"when it was made in a room"},{"text":"you could rent for free."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-053","slides":[{"text":"public access had talk shows and cooking shows"},{"text":"and puppet shows and psychic hotlines"},{"text":"and fitness programs and political roundtables"},{"text":"and shows that were just one person"},{"text":"sitting in a chair"},{"text":"with something to say."},{"text":"late nite local."}]},{"id":"lnl-054","slides":[{"text":"the production value is one camera"},{"text":"and whatever was in the supply closet."},{"text":"the ideas are unlimited."},{"text":"the follow-through is optional."},{"text":"late nite local."}]}],"audio":[{"filename":"celadonplaza---271.mp3","title":"271","artist":"Celadonplaza","url":"https://celadonplaza.bandcamp.com/track/--271","license":"by"},{"filename":"celadonplaza---272.mp3","title":"272","artist":"Celadonplaza","url":"https://celadonplaza.bandcamp.com/track/--272","license":"by"},{"filename":"celadonplaza---273.mp3","title":"273","artist":"Celadonplaza","url":"https://celadonplaza.bandcamp.com/track/--273","license":"by"},{"filename":"celadonplaza---276.mp3","title":"276","artist":"Celadonplaza","url":"https://celadonplaza.bandcamp.com/track/--276","license":"by"},{"filename":"experimentalrecords-return.mp3","title":"Return","artist":"Experimentalrecords","url":"https://experimentalrecords.bandcamp.com/track/return","license":"by"},{"filename":"experimentalrecords-perfume-and-cigarettes.mp3","title":"Perfume And Cigarettes","artist":"Experimentalrecords","url":"https://experimentalrecords.bandcamp.com/track/perfume-and-cigarettes","license":"by"},{"filename":"experimentalrecords-closing-shift-ft.mp3","title":"Closing Shift Ft","artist":"Experimentalrecords","url":"h